<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osun State</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osun State is a state in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, created in 1991 from part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo</a> State, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osogbo">Osogbo</a>. It covers much of the old Ijesha and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ife">Ife</a> lands, including Ilesa and Ile-Ife, regarded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> as their ancestral home. It takes its name from the Osun river and goddess, whose sacred grove at Osogbo is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osun-state.jpg" alt="Osun State" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: S.aderogba · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Erin-ijesha-water-fall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
